<title>NEW ZEALAND: Port of Tauranga CEO to resign.</title>
<headline>Port of Tauranga CEO to resign.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Port of Tauranga said on Thursday that Chief Executive John Halling would resign after almost seven years with the company.</p>
<p>The Chairman, Fraser McKenzie, said Halling had indicated it was time to seek new challenges.</p>
<p>McKenzie said Halling's time with the company had been one of significant change in port performance, infrastructure and volume growth.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
